# Line endings: the repository stores LF, and the working tree uses LF too, on every OS.
# This overrides each developer's core.autocrlf, so a Windows checkout never turns files into CRLF
# and a commit can never again show a whole file as changed because of line endings.
# Why LF in the working tree: Dockerfile, Makefile and shell scripts must be LF on Linux, and the engine's
# rule pack hash and golden files must be byte-identical on every machine (QUORMA game-engine AGENTS.md).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts need CRLF
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary files: never convert
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.jar binary
*.zip binary
